==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mk|sla-pro|*krьstъ}}, ultimately from {{etyl|la|sh}} {{m|la|crux}} (cruci), "cross, stake" or ''crio'' "torment". The Slavic suffix "t" is possibly influenced by {{etyl|grc|sh}} {{m|grc|Χριστός}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kr̂st/|lang=sh}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=кр̏ст|c|krst|kȑst}}

# {{label|sh|Serbia|Bosnia}} [[cross]], [[crucifix]] (also figuratively)

